{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791122163,"nonce":"iecYY3uvJqbph0bBBVFDykVUXFs=","title":"GenericFont::System resolves to Helvetica on macOS, not the real system face","message":"load_generic_with_style maps GenericFont::System to fontdb's\nFamily::SansSerif, which on macOS resolves to Helvetica. Browsers\nresolve system-ui to SF Pro.\n\nThe visible consequence: Helvetica's metrics (ascender 1577, descender\n-471, cap height 1469 at 2048 units/em) put capitals about 1.25px above\ncentre in a 14px button under CSS half-leading. SF Pro's centre them. So\nblinc_cn button text does not sit centred.\n\nThe ashui session now resolves system-ui, and text with no family, to\n\".SF NS\" / \"SF Pro\" in its binding, and Segoe UI on Windows. Blinc may\nwant the same in the registry.\n\nBlocked on the variable-font weight gap: SF Pro's only macOS face is\nSFNS.ttf, a variable font, and blinc_text cannot set a wght axis, so\nswitching to it would draw regular at every weight. See the font\nvariation issue. ashui uses Helvetica Neue in the meantime, which has\nstatic Regular, Medium and Bold and whose metrics also centre capitals.","files":null}]}